{{Quote|That's Appenza Peak. It's the most famous mountain on Alderaan.''"<br />"''It's beautiful.''"<br />"''And treacherous. That mountain is the one that took my lungs and heart.|Breha Organa and Padmé Amidala|<ref name="Queen's Shadow">''[[Queen's Shadow]]''</ref>}}
'''Appenza Peak''' was the most famous [[Water|snow]]-capped [[mountain]] on the [[planet]] [[Alderaan]], visible from the [[capital]] [[Aldera]]. Although it was not Alderaan's highest mountain, its silhouette featured on the [[Unidentified flag|flag]] of the capital [[Unidentified region|region]]. Many [[Alderaanian]] fairy tales began with a spirit flying away from its home on the mountain to choose an adventurer, and religious [[pilgrim]]s claimed it was possible to commune with [[the Force]] at its summit. The climb to the mountain's summit was considered relatively easy, and hundreds made the trek every [[Standard year|year]].

It was traditional for the [[Prince|heir]] to the [[Alderaanian monarchy]] to climb the mountain solo for their [[Challenge of the Body]]. During her Challenge, then-Princess [[Breha Organa]] was severely injured in a [[The accident|fall]] while descending the peak, only surviving due to the quick actions of the [[Alderaan Guard|royal guards]] supervising from a distance. As [[Queen]], Breha's adopted daughter [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia]] asked her mother to accompany her for her Challenge of the Body. Along with the rest of the planet, Appenza Peak was [[Destruction of Alderaan|destroyed]] by the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|first Death Star]] in [[1 BBY]].

==Description==
Appenza Peak was a [[Water|snowcapped]] [[mountain]]<ref name="Queen's Shadow" /> located in the [[capital]] [[Unidentified region|region]] of the [[Core Worlds]] [[planet]] [[Alderaan]]. It was visible from the capital [[city]] of [[Aldera]]. The climb to its summit was considered a relatively easy one, such that hundreds made the trek every [[Standard year|year]].<ref name="LPOA" />

Although not the tallest mountain on Alderaan, Appenza Peak held immense cultural significance to the [[Alderaanian]]s. Its silhouette featured on the [[Unidentified flag|flag]] of the capital region, and many Alderaanian fairy tales began with a spirit flying away from its home on the mountain to choose an adventurer. Religious [[pilgrim]]s claimed that it was possible to commune with [[the Force]] on Appenza Peak's summit. As part of the three challenges the [[Prince|heir]] to the [[Alderaanian monarchy]] was required to undergo to prove themselves worthy, it became traditional for heirs to climb Appenza Peak for their [[Challenge of the Body]], which they could do either solo or taking along one companion.<ref name="LPOA" />

==History==
{{Quote|Look. That's Appenza Peak. Your mother climbed that mountain to prove she was ready to become crown princess of Alderaan.''"<br />"''All by herself?''"<br />"''All by herself.|Bail and Leia Organa|<ref name="LPOA" />}}
Alderaan, a [[Core Worlds]] [[planet]], came to be ruled by a hereditary [[monarchy]] under the [[House of Organa]] from the capital city of Aldera, which was constructed near Appenza Peak in the same planetary region and which enjoyed a magnificent view of the mountain. Heirs to the [[throne]] were required to prove their worth through three challenges, one each of the [[Challenge of the Heart|Heart]], [[Challenge of the Mind|Mind]], and Body. Appenza Peak became a crucial part of the Challenge of the Body, as a tradition developed that the heir climb it to fulfill the challenge. In the final [[Standard decade|decades]] of the [[Galactic Republic]], Princess [[Breha Organa]] suffered a near-[[Death|fatal]] [[The accident|fall]] while descending Appenza Peak during her Challenge of the Body, saved from death only by the swift actions of [[Alderaan Guard|royal guards]] supervising from a distance. The injuries took Breha's [[lung]]s and [[heart]], leaving her with [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] [[pulmonodes]]. Due to the stress inflicted on her body, after she became [[Monarch of Alderaan|Queen]], Breha and her [[Marriage|consort]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail]] decided they would adopt a [[Youngling|child]] instead of Breha [[Reproduction|bearing]] one herself.<ref name="LPOA" />

In [[28 BBY]],<ref name="QS Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Queen's Shadow]]'' to [[28 BBY]].</ref> Bail and Breha invited recently appointed [[Naboo]] [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] for a state visit. Amidala, who had formerly been the [[Monarch of Naboo|elected]] [[Queen]] of Naboo, bonded with Breha. During a breakfast at the [[Royal Palace of Alderaan|Royal Palace]], Breha pointed out Appenza Peak. Amidala remarked on the mountain's beauty, and Breha stated that it was also treacherous, noting the injuries she had received climbing it. Amidala also looked at a [[Unidentified Appenza Peak painting|landscape painting]] of Appenza Peak.<ref name="Queen's Shadow" /> In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="SWGA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> the Organas adopted Amidala's newborn daughter [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia]] after her mother's death and the rise of the [[Galactic Empire]] from the ashes of the Republic.<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref> When Leia came of age at sixteen and underwent [[Leia Organa's Day of Demand|her]] [[Day of Demand]], she swore to undertake the Challenges of the Body, Heart, and Mind, promising to undergo [[pathfinding]] training to prepare herself to climb Appenza Peak solo. The following period saw Leia discover that her [[parent]]s were involved in plotting a rebellion against the Empire and get involved herself, although she lost her first romantic partner, fellow Alderaanian [[Kier Domadi]], whom she had met in her pathfinding class. When it came time for Leia to carry out her Challenge of the Body, she invited her mother to join her as her one companion.<ref name="LPOA" />

In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date GA" /> the Empire discovered the Organas were aligned with the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. Leia, [[Secret mission to Tatooine|captured]]<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref> after fleeing the [[Battle of Scarif]] with the [[Death Star plans]],<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> was brought on board the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], an enormous [[battle station]] with a planet-killing [[superlaser]], and was forced to watch as Alderaan was [[Destruction of Alderaan|destroyed]]. The Death Star was shortly [[Battle of Yavin|destroyed]] itself in a heroic effort by the Rebellion. At the [[Royal Award Ceremony]] to honor the [[Heroes of Yavin|heroes]] who had made it possible,<ref name="ANH" /> Leia thought about what she had lost, remembering climbing Appenza Peak before turning her attention to the present and the continued [[Galactic Civil War|war]].<ref name="Queen's Peril">''[[Queen's Peril]]''</ref> Leia later remembered Appenza Peak when thinking about all the small things she lost when Alderaan was destroyed.<ref name="The Princess and the Scoundrel">''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]''</ref>

In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Princess and the Scoundrel date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[The Princess and the Scoundrel]]'' to [[4 ABY]].</ref> while on [[Madurs]] during her honeymoon with her husband [[Han Solo]], Leia noted that as much as people loved a love story that the only thing people loved more than a hero was a fallen hero. That the more she was celebrated the more people would look for her flaws to exploit and use them to topple her image. This reminded Leia of her mother and her fall from Appenza Peak, and Leia realized that every moment of joy was only raising her higher so that when she inevitably fell it would be harder.<ref name="The Princess and the Scoundrel" />

==Behind the scenes==
Appenza Peak first appeared in the [[2017]] young-adult novel ''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]'', written by [[Claudia Gray]].<ref name="LPOA" /> It was first pictured in the novel's manga adaptation, ''[[Leia Organa: Ordeal of the Princess]]'', which was written and illustrated by [[Haruichi]].<ref name="Ordeal">''[[Leia Organa: Ordeal of the Princess]]''</ref>

